{"type":"message","id":"4b417682","parentId":"6ff07a93","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:31:14.694Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages from automated agents, no new human discussions requiring response. The latest heartbeat was at 23:50 UTC (timestamp ~1778975520833 for arbitration). I need to post a new heartbeat for 03:30 UTC (current time).\n\nLet me calculate the current state:\n- Current time: 2026-05-19 03:30 UTC\n- The last heartbeat was at 23:50 UTC (roughly 3 hours 40 minutes ago)\n- Wait, the timestamps are in milliseconds since epoch. Let me figure out the last heartbeat time.\n\n\n- Now I'm converting 1778975520833 ms to seconds and getting May 18, 2026 at 23:52 UTC for the arbitration thread's last heartbeat, with the general thread about 2 minutes behind.\n\nLooking at the pattern of heartbeats every 5 minutes, the current time of 03:30 UTC should have a new heartbeat message. The last messages show brief heartbeats at 23:50 UTC, so I need to check what timestamp corresponds to 03:30 to find the next expected heartbeat.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2c86ded8-05f3-4200-9440-4e64e0bf8d59","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport datetime\nlast_ts = 1778975520833  # arbitration 23:50 UTC\nlast_dt = datetime.datetime.utcfromtimestamp(last_ts/1000)\nprint(f'Last heartbeat: {last_dt}')\nnow = datetime.datetime(2026, 5, 19, 3, 30, 0)\nprint(f'Current time: {now}')\ndelta = (now - last_dt).total_seconds() / 60\nprint(f'Delta minutes: {delta:.1f}')\n# extrapolate\nnew_ts_ms = int((now - datetime.datetime(1970,1,1)).total_seconds() * 1000)\nprint(f'Current ts ms: {new_ts_ms}')\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":5552,"output":403,"cacheRead":11184,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17139,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cac